From: SJ Park <sj@kernel.org>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 09:56:57 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Docs/mm/damon/maintainer-profile: further wordsmith

Signed-off-by: SJ Park <sj@kernel.org>
---
 Documentation/mm/damon/maintainer-profile.rst | 33 +++++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/mm/damon/maintainer-profile.rst b/Documentation/mm/damon/maintainer-profile.rst
index 3a0ac10536c60..8e7fb120a5bdc 100644
--- a/Documentation/mm/damon/maintainer-profile.rst
+++ b/Documentation/mm/damon/maintainer-profile.rst
@@ -9,12 +9,12 @@ DAMON' section of 'MAINTAINERS' file.
 The mailing lists for the subsystem are damon@lists.linux.dev and
 linux-mm@kvack.org.
 
-Non-hotfix patches should be made against the mm/damon.git `for-next
-<https://git.kernel.org/mm/damon/h/for-next>`_ tree.  Hotfix patches should be
-made against the mm/damon.git `for-next-fixes
+Non-urgent patches should be made against the damon.git `for-next
+<https://git.kernel.org/mm/damon/h/for-next>`_ tree.  Urgent patches should be
+made against the damon.git `for-next-fixes
 <https://git.kernel.org/mm/damon/h/for-next-fixes>`_ tree.  If there is a
-reason to not use those branches as the baseline of the patch, please
-explicitly explain the reason and what baseline is used.
+reason to not use those branches as the baseline of the patch, please explain
+the reason and what baseline is used.
 
 Patches should be posted to the mailing lists whenever possible.
 
@@ -23,8 +23,6 @@ Submit checklist addendum
 
 When making DAMON changes, you should do below.
 
-- Ensure the patch can be ``git am``-ed on the latest mm/damon.git for-next
-  tree.
 - Build changes related outputs including kernel and documents.
 - Ensure the builds introduce no new errors or warnings.
 - Run and ensure no new failures for DAMON `selftests
@@ -45,11 +43,20 @@ Key cycle dates
 
 Patches can be sent to and reviewed on the mailing lists anytime.
 
-Patches that are reviewed and no problem is found will be merged into
-mm/damon.git ``for-next-fixes`` or ``for-next`` trees.  The merge destination
-is decided based on whether the patch is a hotfix or not.  Being merged into
-damon.git is only for additional review and testing.  All patches in damon.git
-can be reviewed, modified and dropped at any time.
+Patches that are sufficiently reviewed will be merged into damon.git
+``for-next-fixes`` or ``for-next`` trees.  The destination tree is decided
+based on the urgency of the patches.  The merge destination is decided based on
+whether the patch is a hotfix or not.  Being merged into damon.git is only for
+additional review and testing.  All patches in damon.git can be reviewed,
+modified and dropped at any time.
+
+Patches in ``for-next-fixes`` tree stay there for at least one week, for
+additional review and testing.  After that, those will be pull-requested to the
+mainline.
+
+Patches in ``for-next`` tree stay there at least two weeks, for additional
+review and testing.  After that, those will be pull-requested to the mainline,
+in the next merge window.
 
 ``for-next`` tree is closed for new patches from -rc6 release to next -rc1
 release.
@@ -57,7 +64,7 @@ release.
 Review cadence
 --------------
 
-The DAMON maintainer usually works in a flexible way, except early morning in PT
+DAMON maintainer usually works in a flexible way, except early morning in PT
 (Pacific Time).  The response to patches will occasionally be slow.  Do not
 hesitate to send a ping if you have not heard back within a week of sending a
 patch.
-- 
2.47.3

